## 15. Success measurement

| Outcome | KPI |
|---|---|
| Migration completeness | Migrated / in-scope subscribers |
| Data integrity | Successful validation rate |
| Payment readiness | Payment-ready subscriber rate |
| Customer continuity | Subscriber retention after migration |
| Billing continuity | First-cycle billing success |
| Financial control | Duplicate billing incidents |
| Reconciliation | Source-to-target match rate |
| Operational quality | Migration exception rate |
| Customer experience | Reauthorization completion rate |
| Stability | Post-migration incident rate |

### Suggested migration acceptance criteria

Set thresholds with the merchant before execution.

Examples:

- All in-scope records have traceable source identifiers.
- All activated subscriptions have approved target configuration.
- No unapproved duplicate billing.
- All payment credentials are either explicitly validated for portability or reauthorized.
- Billing amounts and next billing dates are reconciled.
- Financial exceptions are documented and assigned.
- Merchant signs off on cutover and hypercare completion.

Do not use arbitrary success percentages as universal FlexiBill product guarantees.

